  "query_preview": "..\n\nA rather benign pattern this week for southeastern Arizona as \nthe jet stream remains to the north. While temperatures have \nmoderated from this weekend's activity, crossing shortwaves to \nthe north will keep temperatures below normal through the week.\n\nEnsembles continue to show an upper level circulation breaking\noff from the main flow this weekend into early next week over\nsouthern Arizona to northern Baja.Sonora. There remain \ndifferences in the ensemble cores with the GEFS mean flow \nfavoring a stronger low with a greater probability of \nprecipitation and a weaker low with lower precipitation chances\nfrom the EPS/GEPS. Overall the grand ensemble members favor a \ndry solution as does the current forecast, with very low but \nnon- zero chances of rain. Breezy easterly winds will be \npossible this weekend as the circulation drops to the south, \nwith advisory level winds looking unlikely overall at this \nmoment.",
